WEBVTT

00:00.650 --> 00:02.630
So I've got an
arbitrary triangle here.

00:02.630 --> 00:04.830
We'll call it triangle ABC.

00:04.830 --> 00:07.130
And what I want to do
is look at the midpoints

00:07.130 --> 00:08.840
of each of the sides of ABC.

00:08.840 --> 00:12.050
So this is the midpoint of
one of the sides, of side BC.

00:12.050 --> 00:17.160
Let's call that point D. Let's
call this midpoint E. And let's

00:17.160 --> 00:20.720
call this midpoint
right over here F.

00:20.720 --> 00:22.320
And since it's the
midpoint, we know

00:22.320 --> 00:25.380
that the distance between BD
is equal to the distance from D

00:25.380 --> 00:28.210
to C. So this distance is
equal to this distance.

00:28.210 --> 00:31.380
We know that AE is equal
to EC, so this distance

00:31.380 --> 00:32.970
is equal to that distance.

00:32.970 --> 00:35.620
And we know that
AF is equal to FB,

00:35.620 --> 00:39.150
so this distance is
equal to this distance.

00:39.150 --> 00:41.399
Instead of drawing medians
going from these midpoints

00:41.399 --> 00:42.940
to the vertices,
what I want to do is

00:42.940 --> 00:46.090
I want to connect these
midpoints and see what happens.

00:46.090 --> 00:48.830
So if I connect them, I
clearly have three points.

00:48.830 --> 00:52.970
So if you connect three
non-linear points like this,

00:52.970 --> 00:55.710
you will get another triangle.

00:55.710 --> 00:59.470
And this triangle that's formed
from the midpoints of the sides

00:59.470 --> 01:02.623
of this larger triangle-- we
call this a medial triangle.

01:06.800 --> 01:08.880
And that's all nice
and cute by itself.

01:08.880 --> 01:10.060
But what we're going
to see in this video

01:10.060 --> 01:11.590
is that the medial
triangle actually

01:11.590 --> 01:13.800
has some very neat properties.

01:13.800 --> 01:15.210
What we're actually
going to show

01:15.210 --> 01:19.290
is that it divides any triangle
into four smaller triangles

01:19.290 --> 01:21.220
that are congruent
to each other,

01:21.220 --> 01:24.530
that all four of these triangles
are identical to each other.

01:24.530 --> 01:26.610
And they're all similar
to the larger triangle.

01:26.610 --> 01:28.430
And you could think
of them each as having

01:28.430 --> 01:31.320
1/4 of the area of
the larger triangle.

01:31.320 --> 01:33.650
So let's go about proving it.

01:33.650 --> 01:35.700
So first, let's focus
on this triangle down

01:35.700 --> 01:37.310
here, triangle CDE.

01:37.310 --> 01:40.200
And it looks similar
to the larger triangle,

01:40.200 --> 01:42.450
to triangle CBA.

01:42.450 --> 01:44.964
But let's prove it to ourselves.

01:44.964 --> 01:47.130
So one thing we can say is,
well, look, both of them

01:47.130 --> 01:49.570
share this angle
right over here.

01:49.570 --> 01:53.650
Both the larger triangle,
triangle CBA, has this angle.

01:53.650 --> 01:56.630
And the smaller triangle,
CDE, has this angle.

01:56.630 --> 01:58.460
So they definitely
share that angle.

01:58.460 --> 02:00.950
And then let's think about
the ratios of the sides.

02:00.950 --> 02:14.240
We know that the ratio of CD
to CB is equal to 1 over 2.

02:14.240 --> 02:18.350
This is 1/2 of this entire
side, is equal to 1 over 2.

02:18.350 --> 02:22.980
And that's the same thing
as the ratio of CE to CA.

02:22.980 --> 02:27.040
CE is exactly 1/2 of CA,
because E is the midpoint.

02:27.040 --> 02:30.880
It's equal to CE over CA.

02:30.880 --> 02:33.295
So we have an angle,
corresponding angles that

02:33.295 --> 02:35.150
are congruent, and
then the ratios

02:35.150 --> 02:37.840
of two corresponding sides
on either side of that angle

02:37.840 --> 02:38.480
are the same.

02:38.480 --> 02:45.010
CD over CB is 1/2, CE over CA
is 1/2, and the angle in between

02:45.010 --> 02:46.120
is congruent.

02:46.120 --> 03:03.460
So by SAS similarity, we
know that triangle CDE

03:03.460 --> 03:08.070
is similar to triangle CBA.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.860
And just from that, you can
get some interesting results.

03:14.860 --> 03:16.318
Because then we
know that the ratio

03:16.318 --> 03:20.230
of this side of the smaller
triangle to the longer triangle

03:20.230 --> 03:21.880
is also going to be 1/2.

03:21.880 --> 03:23.880
Because the other two
sides have a ratio of 1/2,

03:23.880 --> 03:25.710
and we're dealing with
similar triangles.

03:25.710 --> 03:27.860
So this is going
to be 1/2 of that.

03:27.860 --> 03:32.750
And we know 1/2 of AB is just
going to be the length of FA.

03:32.750 --> 03:34.960
So we know that this
length right over here

03:34.960 --> 03:37.911
is going to be the
same as FA or FB.

03:37.911 --> 03:39.910
And we get that straight
from similar triangles.

03:39.910 --> 03:49.290
Because these are similar,
we know that DE over BA

03:49.290 --> 03:51.730
has got to be equal
to these ratios,

03:51.730 --> 03:54.650
the other corresponding
sides, which is equal to 1/2.

03:54.650 --> 03:57.580
And so that's how we got
that right over there.

03:57.580 --> 04:01.395
Now let's think about
this triangle up here.

04:04.070 --> 04:05.187
We could call it BDF.

04:07.800 --> 04:09.610
So first of all, if
we compare triangle

04:09.610 --> 04:12.930
BDF to the larger
triangle, they both share

04:12.930 --> 04:15.780
this angle right
over here, angle ABC.

04:15.780 --> 04:17.810
They both have that
angle in common.

04:17.810 --> 04:20.279
And we're going to have
the exact same argument.

04:20.279 --> 04:21.714
You can just look
at this diagram.

04:21.714 --> 04:27.120
And you know that the ratio
of BA-- let me do it this way.

04:27.120 --> 04:33.950
The ratio of BF to
BA is equal to 1/2,

04:33.950 --> 04:36.725
which is also the
ratio of BD to BC.

04:40.820 --> 04:42.830
The ratio of this
to that is the same

04:42.830 --> 04:45.710
as the ratio of this
to that, which is 1/2.

04:45.710 --> 04:47.360
Because BD is 1/2 of
this whole length.

04:47.360 --> 04:49.500
BF is 1/2 of that whole length.

04:49.500 --> 04:51.860
And so you have
corresponding sides

04:51.860 --> 04:53.860
have the same ratio
on the two triangles,

04:53.860 --> 04:55.450
and they share an
angle in between.

04:55.450 --> 05:03.010
So once again, by
SAS similarity,

05:03.010 --> 05:07.980
we know that triangle--
I'll write it

05:07.980 --> 05:18.750
this way-- DBF is
similar to triangle CBA.

05:25.129 --> 05:27.420
And once again, we use this
exact same kind of argument

05:27.420 --> 05:28.435
that we did with this triangle.

05:28.435 --> 05:31.060
Well, if it's similar, the ratio
of all the corresponding sides

05:31.060 --> 05:32.070
have to be the same.

05:32.070 --> 05:33.380
And that ratio is 1/2.

05:33.380 --> 05:35.680
So the ratio of this
side to this side,

05:35.680 --> 05:41.420
the ratio of FD to
AC, has to be 1/2.

05:41.420 --> 05:44.100
Or FD has to be 1/2 of AC.

05:44.100 --> 05:46.750
And 1/2 of AC is just
the length of AE.

05:46.750 --> 05:50.710
So that is just going to be
that length right over there.

05:50.710 --> 05:52.700
I think you see
where this is going.

05:52.700 --> 05:55.470
And also, because it's similar,
all of the corresponding angles

05:55.470 --> 05:56.490
have to be the same.

05:56.490 --> 05:58.990
And we know that
the larger triangle

05:58.990 --> 06:00.870
has a yellow angle
right over there.

06:00.870 --> 06:03.766
So we'd have that yellow
angle right over here.

06:03.766 --> 06:05.140
And this triangle
right over here

06:05.140 --> 06:07.440
was also similar to
the larger triangle.

06:07.440 --> 06:09.760
So it will have that same
angle measure up here.

06:09.760 --> 06:12.660
We already showed that
in this first part.

06:12.660 --> 06:14.864
So now let's go to
this third triangle.

06:14.864 --> 06:16.030
I think you see the pattern.

06:16.030 --> 06:18.155
I'm sure you might be able
to just pause this video

06:18.155 --> 06:19.770
and prove it for yourself.

06:19.770 --> 06:25.800
But we see that the
ratio of AF over AB

06:25.800 --> 06:28.776
is going to be the
same as the ratio of AE

06:28.776 --> 06:33.380
over AC, which is equal to 1/2.

06:33.380 --> 06:36.970
So we have two corresponding
sides where the ratio is 1/2,

06:36.970 --> 06:38.960
from the smaller
to larger triangle.

06:38.960 --> 06:41.510
And they share a common angle.

06:41.510 --> 06:44.450
They share this angle in
between the two sides.

06:44.450 --> 06:47.470
So by SAS similarity--
this is getting repetitive

06:47.470 --> 06:59.563
now-- we know that triangle
EFA is similar to triangle CBA.

07:03.280 --> 07:05.460
And so the ratio of all
of the corresponding sides

07:05.460 --> 07:06.680
need to be 1/2.

07:06.680 --> 07:10.000
So the ratio of FE to
BC needs to be 1/2,

07:10.000 --> 07:13.630
or FE needs to be 1/2 of that,
which is just the length of BD.

07:13.630 --> 07:17.720
So this is just going to be
that length right over there.

07:17.720 --> 07:19.500
And you can also
say that since we've

07:19.500 --> 07:22.380
shown that this triangle, this
triangle, and this triangle--

07:22.380 --> 07:24.005
we haven't talked
about this middle one

07:24.005 --> 07:26.640
yet-- they're all similar
to the larger triangle.

07:26.640 --> 07:28.890
So they're also all going
to be similar to each other.

07:28.890 --> 07:32.080
So they're all going to have
the same corresponding angles.

07:32.080 --> 07:34.332
So if the larger triangle
had this yellow angle here,

07:34.332 --> 07:35.790
then all of the
triangles are going

07:35.790 --> 07:38.520
to have this yellow
angle right over there.

07:38.520 --> 07:40.620
And if the larger triangle
had this blue angle

07:40.620 --> 07:43.280
right over here, then in
the corresponding vertex,

07:43.280 --> 07:46.005
all of the triangles are
going to have that blue angle.

07:46.005 --> 07:47.880
All of the ones that
we've shown are similar.

07:47.880 --> 07:50.750
We haven't thought about this
middle triangle just yet.

07:50.750 --> 07:52.780
And of course, if this
is similar to the whole,

07:52.780 --> 07:56.310
it'll also have this
angle at this vertex

07:56.310 --> 07:58.820
right over here, because this
corresponds to that vertex,

07:58.820 --> 08:01.152
based on the similarity.

08:01.152 --> 08:02.068
So that's interesting.

08:02.068 --> 08:06.640
Now let's compare the
triangles to each other.

08:06.640 --> 08:09.240
We've now shown that
all of these triangles

08:09.240 --> 08:11.200
have the exact same three sides.

08:11.200 --> 08:14.520
Has this blue side-- or
actually, this one-mark side,

08:14.520 --> 08:16.760
this two-mark side, and
this three-mark side.

08:16.760 --> 08:18.220
One mark, two mark, three mark.

08:18.220 --> 08:19.910
One mark, two mark, three mark.

08:19.910 --> 08:22.670
And that even applies
to this middle triangle

08:22.670 --> 08:24.020
right over here.

08:24.020 --> 08:35.049
So by side-side-side
congruency, we now know--

08:35.049 --> 08:38.000
and we want to be careful to get
our corresponding sides right--

08:38.000 --> 08:45.220
we now know that triangle CDE
is congruent to triangle DBF.

08:49.707 --> 08:51.290
I want to get the
corresponding sides.

08:51.290 --> 08:51.980
I'm looking at the colors.

08:51.980 --> 08:54.420
I went from yellow to magenta
to blue, yellow, magenta,

08:54.420 --> 08:58.910
to blue, which is going to
be congruent to triangle

08:58.910 --> 09:04.921
EFA, which is going to be
congruent to this triangle

09:04.921 --> 09:05.420
in here.

09:05.420 --> 09:07.180
But we want to make
sure that we're

09:07.180 --> 09:09.480
getting the right
corresponding sides here.

09:09.480 --> 09:11.010
So to make sure we
do that, we just

09:11.010 --> 09:12.770
have to think about the angles.

09:12.770 --> 09:15.100
So we know-- and
this is interesting--

09:15.100 --> 09:18.330
that because the interior
angles of a triangle

09:18.330 --> 09:20.820
add up to 180 degrees,
we know this magenta

09:20.820 --> 09:24.600
angle plus this blue angle plus
this yellow angle equal 180.

09:24.600 --> 09:27.010
Here, we have the blue
angle and the magenta angle,

09:27.010 --> 09:29.610
and clearly they will
all add up to 180.

09:29.610 --> 09:31.600
So you must have the blue angle.

09:31.600 --> 09:33.850
The blue angle must
be right over here.

09:33.850 --> 09:37.300
Same argument-- yellow
angle and blue angle,

09:37.300 --> 09:39.510
we must have the magenta
angle right over here.

09:39.510 --> 09:40.690
They add up to 180.

09:40.690 --> 09:42.250
So this must be
the magenta angle.

09:42.250 --> 09:44.630
And then finally,
magenta and blue-- this

09:44.630 --> 09:47.192
must be the yellow
angle right over there.

09:47.192 --> 09:48.900
And so when we wrote
the congruency here,

09:48.900 --> 09:50.890
we started at CDE.

09:50.890 --> 09:53.710
We went yellow, magenta, blue.

09:53.710 --> 09:57.190
So over here, we're going
to go yellow, magenta, blue.

09:57.190 --> 09:59.544
So it's going to be
congruent to triangle FED.

10:05.440 --> 10:06.620
And so that's pretty cool.

10:06.620 --> 10:09.472
We just showed that all
three, that this triangle,

10:09.472 --> 10:11.430
this triangle, this
triangle, and that triangle

10:11.430 --> 10:12.530
are congruent.

10:12.530 --> 10:14.830
And also, we can look
at the corresponding--

10:14.830 --> 10:17.680
and that they all have
ratios relative to-- they're

10:17.680 --> 10:20.520
all similar to the larger
triangle, to triangle ABC.

10:20.520 --> 10:23.430
And that the ratio between
the sides is 1 to 2.

10:23.430 --> 10:25.940
And also, because we've looked
at corresponding angles,

10:25.940 --> 10:30.520
we see, for example,
that this angle

10:30.520 --> 10:31.770
is the same as that angle.

10:31.770 --> 10:33.860
So if you viewed DC
or if you viewed BC

10:33.860 --> 10:35.710
as a transversal,
all of a sudden

10:35.710 --> 10:40.440
it becomes pretty clear that FD
is going to be parallel to AC,

10:40.440 --> 10:43.130
because the corresponding
angles are congruent.

10:43.130 --> 10:46.900
So this is going to be parallel
to that right over there.

10:46.900 --> 10:49.060
And then you could use
that same exact argument

10:49.060 --> 10:51.780
to say, well, then this
side, because once again,

10:51.780 --> 10:56.080
corresponding angles
here and here-- you

10:56.080 --> 10:58.490
could say that
this is going to be

10:58.490 --> 11:01.750
parallel to that
right over there.

11:01.750 --> 11:06.360
And then finally, you make
the same argument over here.

11:06.360 --> 11:08.820
I want to make sure I get the
right corresponding angles.

11:08.820 --> 11:12.060
You have this line
and this line.

11:12.060 --> 11:13.850
And this angle
corresponds to that angle.

11:13.850 --> 11:14.980
They're the same.

11:14.980 --> 11:21.410
So this DE must
be parallel to BA.

11:21.410 --> 11:25.280
So that's another neat property
of this medial triangle,

11:25.280 --> 11:27.409
[? I thought. ?]
All of these things

11:27.409 --> 11:29.950
just jump out when you just try
to do something fairly simple

11:29.950 --> 11:32.180
with a triangle.
